\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Every point on nmap's frontier is beaten by a \textsf  {netsanity}{} configuration warm, and the configuration that beats it cold is the ablation that turns the contributed technique off.} Speed against completeness for all eleven discovery conditions in both cache arms; medians with bootstrap 95\% intervals at 10{,}000 resamples, $n$ on every point. Of nmap's eight configurations exactly one is non-dominated in either arm --- privileged \texttt  {-T5} --- so the timing sweep that was in the protocol to make the comparison fair produces one competitor and seven dominated points. Warm, all three \textsf  {netsanity}{} configurations sit inside the shaded quadrant; cold, only the shared-budget ablation does, and the adaptive default this paper is about sits at recall 0.80 and loses to \texttt  {-T5} outright (Section~\ref {sec:h2}).}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pareto}{{1}{2}{\textbf {Every point on nmap's frontier is beaten by a \netsanity {} configuration warm, and the configuration that beats it cold is the ablation that turns the contributed technique off.} Speed against completeness for all eleven discovery conditions in both cache arms; medians with bootstrap 95\% intervals at 10{,}000 resamples, $n$ on every point. Of nmap's eight configurations exactly one is non-dominated in either arm --- privileged \texttt {-T5} --- so the timing sweep that was in the protocol to make the comparison fair produces one competitor and seven dominated points. Warm, all three \netsanity {} configurations sit inside the shaded quadrant; cold, only the shared-budget ablation does, and the adaptive default this paper is about sits at recall 0.80 and loses to \texttt {-T5} outright (Section~\ref {sec:h2})}{figure.1}{}}
